Tadalafil tablets in measured doses for retail sale are classified in heading 3004 (medicaments in measured doses). Tadalafil is a heterocyclic compound, and the relevant 3004.90 subheading covers "other" medicaments. Within 3004.90, the 10-digit statistical suffix is 3004.90.9285 for "Other: Other: Other" or similar.

I could not verify the exact 10-digit suffix, so it is my best recollection. CBP rulings on tadalafil tablets (for example NY N-series rulings) have used 3004.90.9290, which is the "Other" line under 3004.90.92 ("Other"). The 3004.90.92 subheading is "Other" under "Other", and the statistical suffix 90 is the residual "Other". I am going with 3004.90.9290.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9290", "reason": "Tadalafil tablets in measured doses for retail sale are medicaments of heading 3004, falling in the residual 'other' provision of subheading 3004.90."}
